    "reason": "The profile takes exactly one web-bot-auth signature and one Signature-Agent member per request (RFC 9421 section 3.2.1). Web Bot Auth section 5.2.2 permits more than one signature; the profile does not accept one."
  },
  "$comment": "The sig1 label is byte-identical to positive/001-single-signer-request.json, and the sig2 label is a second valid signature over the same request from another identity. Each verifies on its own against its own directory, so a verifier that loops over every label and accepts when each verifies has skipped the count check. The profile reports signature failures with HTTP status codes (Web Bot Auth sections 5.3 and 5.4). A 403 or 429 carries Accept-Signature naming the components and parameters the profile requires, so the signer can sign again. Conformance grades the status code; the accept_signature object describes the header the verifier sends, and the exact serialization is RFC 9421 section 5.1."
